WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.857
Sometimes no answer is the correct system outcome.

00:00:03.857 --> 00:00:10.177
A reliable workflow should be willing to say that it could not verify something from approved evidence.

00:00:10.177 --> 00:00:16.467
For example: I could not verify the return exception from the available policy sources.

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:19.226
Please contact support for confirmation.

00:00:19.882 --> 00:00:25.784
That may feel less impressive than producing a detailed answer, but it is more trustworthy.

00:00:25.784 --> 00:00:30.904
The success criterion is not that the model always says something substantive.

00:00:30.904 --> 00:00:34.740
The success criterion is that the system behaves correctly.

00:00:35.539 --> 00:00:41.411
This becomes especially important in projects involving policy, health, finance,

00:00:41.411 --> 00:00:45.706
or any other domain where unsupported claims can cause harm.

00:00:45.706 --> 00:00:50.086
A safe no-answer result is a feature, not a failure.
